<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market no help at noon.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market no help at noon.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it did not operate in the UK money market despite offering a round of assistance at midday.</p>
<p>The Bank provided provided assistance totalling 1.267 billion stg on Thursday morning, in response to a forecast money market shortage of 2.3 billion pounds.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
